## Control {{controlId}}: Protect the Confidentiality of CUI on Public-Access Systems

**Implementation Status:** {{status}}

This organization protects CUI confidentiality on publicly accessible system components within the {{tenantName}} M365 GCC High tenant through SharePoint sharing restrictions, guest access controls, and Conditional Access policies managed by {{variables.accessControlAdministrator}}.

{{#if sharepointConfigured}}
**SharePoint External Sharing Controls:**
External sharing capability is set to **{{sharingCapability}}**. {{#if externalSharingEnabled}}External sharing is permitted with the following restrictions:{{else}}External sharing is disabled, preventing CUI exposure on public-access surfaces.{{/if}}
- Default sharing link type: **{{defaultSharingLinkType}}**
{{#if ippProtectionEnabled}}- Information Protection Policy (IPP) enforcement is active, applying sensitivity-based access controls to shared content{{/if}}
- Anonymous access links are prohibited for sites containing CUI
- Guest access requires authentication and is scoped to specific sites/documents
{{else}}
SharePoint sharing configuration has not been confirmed. Public access controls for CUI require verification.
{{/if}}

{{#if conditionalAccessActive}}
**Guest Access Enforcement:**
Conditional Access policies enforce additional controls for guest and external users:
{{#each policies}}
- **{{displayName}}** ({{state}}): Requires {{#each grantControls.builtInControls}}{{this}}{{#unless @last}}, {{/unless}}{{/each}}
{{/each}}

Guest users are subject to MFA requirements, compliant device checks, and session restrictions before accessing any organizational content.
{{else}}
Conditional Access enforcement for guest access has not been configured.
{{/if}}

**Responsible Party:** {{variables.accessControlAdministrator}}

**Verification Method:** Examine SharePoint sharing settings, guest access policies, Conditional Access configurations for external users, and anonymous link audit logs.

